# Repo docs are not part of the site. Without this, a zero-config static deploy would
# serve PRD.md, README.md, and AGENTS.md at /PRD.md etc. on the deploy URL.
#
# Blog content DOES land as .md, and this pattern is what keeps it private — do not narrow
# it. A post's Markdown source lives at drafts/<slug>.md while it is unpublished and at
# blog/<slug>.md once it is out, and neither is ever meant to be fetched: the public
# artefact is the generated blog/<slug>.html beside it. `*.md` matches at any depth, so it
# withholds all of them from the deployment upload, which is the whole mechanism by which
# an unpublished draft is unreachable rather than merely unlinked.
#
# This is safe here only because nothing builds: the functions in api/ read and write
# content through the GitHub API, never the deployed filesystem, so a file withheld from
# the upload is a file they never wanted. See AGENTS.md and PRD.md section 7.1.
*.md
